# Vulnerability details

## Impact
delegate call needs to be carefully used. This function can be called in another function as it is an internal function

## Proof of Concept
``` solidity
/**
     * @notice Internal method to delegate execution to another contract
     * @dev It returns to the external caller whatever the implementation returns or forwards reverts
     * @param callee The contract to delegatecall
     * @param data The raw data to delegatecall
     * @return The returned bytes from the delegatecall
     */
    function delegateTo(address callee, bytes memory data) internal returns (bytes memory) {
        // @audit-issue H-01 delegate call needs to be carefully used. This function can be called in another function as it is an internal function.
        // With the address of a malicious contract and data of an encoded amlicious data, an attacker can easily steal funds or take control of this contract.
        // For example calling this function with address (malicious contract) and data signature encodeFunctionSignature("pwn()") would hurt this contract
        // Put checks to verify address being inputted in this contract or avoid using this call if possible.
        (bool success, bytes memory returnData) = callee.delegatecall(data);
        assembly {
            if eq(success, 0) {
                revert(add(returnData, 0x20), returndatasize())
            }
        }
        return returnData;
```

## Tools Used
Remix, Hardhat
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
 - Put checks to verify address being inputted in this contract or avoid using this call if possible.
 - refer to delegate call vulnerability https://www.halborn.com/blog/post/delegatecall-vulnerabilities-in-solidity






