# Vulnerability details

There seems to be a missing nonce check, which could potentially allow an attacker to intercept a valid signature and replay it, granting themselves permission to spend the tokens.

## Impact
There is a lack of nonce check in the `permit` function. This absence of a nonce check can potentially make the signature susceptible to replay attacks. A replay attack occurs when a valid signed message is intercepted and retransmitted with the intention of executing the same action again.


## Proof of Concept

